{
  "case": "weno5_advection_accum",
  "pipeline_kind": "mms_convergence",
  "description": "Solved-trajectory Layer-C case for weno5_advection = div(U*q). Freeze-and-accumulate pattern: U=1 and q=sin(2*pi*x + 1) are frozen (D/dt=0) and a state `acc` integrates the WENO5 flux divergence, so acc(t)=t*div(U*q). Exact = t*2*pi*cos(2*pi*x + 1). The field-level pipeline (build_ode_problem) sweeps N=32->64 and verifies high-order spatial convergence (O(h^5) WENO5). The phase-shifted sine matches the Layer-B MMS; the linear-in-time accumulation isolates the rule's spatial truncation from the solver.",
  "esm": "weno5_advection_pde.esm",
  "grid_refs": [
    "weno_n32.gdd.json",
    "weno_n64.gdd.json"
  ],
  "mms_kind": "sin2pi_shift1_div_accum",
  "t_final": 1.0,
  "convergence": {
    "expected_order": 5.0,
    "min_order": 4.5,
    "comment": "Classical Jiang-Shu WENO5 is O(h^5) in L_inf for smooth data; observed order 5.02 at N=32->64, floor at 4.5 leaves headroom for the nonlinear-weight recovery hit (cf. Layer-B floor of 4.7 over a 4-grid sweep)."
  }
}
